WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.167
The bottom line is a practical one.

00:00:02.247 --> 00:00:07.430
Whenever you find yourself analyzing networks
through subgraph or motif densities,

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:11.154
take one extra step and convert them into graph cumulants.

00:00:11.234 --> 00:00:13.657
You lose nothing in computational cost,

00:00:13.737 --> 00:00:16.610
but you gain sharply higher statistical power,

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:21.232
a trustworthy chi-squared null distribution for
controlling error rates,

00:00:21.312 --> 00:00:25.853
and the ability to draw conclusions even from a
single observed network.

00:00:25.933 --> 00:00:28.742
In short, graph cumulants offer a principled,

00:00:28.822 --> 00:00:34.070
more natural first layer of features for comparing
the local structure of networks.
